<div id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first evaluate our method on the CIFAR-10 dataset using the ResNet-18 model and compare it against existing approaches. As shown in Table <a href="#S4.T1" title="TABLE I ‣ IV-B1 Results on CIFAR-10 ‣ IV-B Results ‣ IV Experiment and Results ‣ RegMix: Adversarial Mutual and Generalization Regularization for Enhancing DNN Robustness" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">I</span></a>, under PGD-10 attacks, our method achieves a robust accuracy of 57.46<math id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>%</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\%</annotation></semantics></math>, outperforming FGSM-PGK by 1.38<math id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>%</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\%</annotation></semantics></math>. Furthermore, as illustrated in Fig. <a href="#S4.F4" title="Fig. 4 ‣ IV-C Performance Analysis ‣ IV Experiment and Results ‣ RegMix: Adversarial Mutual and Generalization Regularization for Enhancing DNN Robustness" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, our method not only achieves higher robustness under the same perturbation settings, but also consistently outperforms FGSM-PGI and FGSM-PGK under stronger <math id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> attacks, including PGD and AA. Under a more challenging perturbation level of <math id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\infty}=16/255" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>255</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\infty}=16/255</annotation></semantics></math>, our method attains 49.42% robust accuracy, exceeding FGSM-PGK by 1.25<math id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>%</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\%</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S4.T2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">TABLE II</span>: </span><span id="S4.T2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Clean and robust accuracy (%) of WideResNet-34-10 on CIFAR-10 under <math id="S4.T2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\infty}=8/255" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>255</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\infty}=8/255</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.T2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16/255" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>255</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16/255</annotation></semantics></math> perturbations. Both best and last checkpoints are reported. Best results are in bold.</span></figcaption>
